---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About - Wrestling Heritage Registry">
  <div class="mb-12 border-b border-slate-200 pb-6">
    <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl mb-4">About the Registry</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">The International Professional Wrestling Heritage Registry (IPWHR)</p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose max-w-none text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
    <p>
      In recognition of professional wrestling as a unique global art form, a medium for athletic storytelling, and a significant cultural force, the International Professional Wrestling Heritage Registry (IPWHR) is established. 
    </p>
    <p>
      The mission of the IPWHR is to identify, categorize, and preserve for future generations a definitive collection of wrestling's most significant moments—both triumphant and tragic. This registry will serve not only as a "hall of fame" for singular achievements but also as a vital educational archive, providing context for the industry's evolution and crucial lessons from its past.
    </p>
    <h3 class="font-bold text-xl mt-8 mb-4">Governing Principles</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Impartiality:</strong> The Registry will operate independently of any single promotion, era, or style. Significance is the sole metric for consideration.</li>
      <li><strong>Global Scope:</strong> Wrestling is a worldwide phenomenon. The Registry will actively seek and preserve significant moments from promotions across the globe.</li>
      <li><strong>Historical Integrity:</strong> The Registry is committed to presenting an honest and complete history of the industry, acknowledging its greatest artistic achievements alongside its most profound ethical failures.</li>
      <li><strong>Educational Purpose:</strong> The primary function of this archive is to provide context and insight for fans, performers, and historians, ensuring the lessons of the past inform the future.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
